t's going on here now  whether  they're violating their own policies i  don't know about that but i do know what  the law says  and as far as what the law says he's  fine to do it  all right there are some republicans  though who disagree with that but  valerie what did you think of the impact  of that speech  well it wasn't just the secretary of  state doing it was also the fact that  they held  much of the ceremony in the white house  in the rose garden  girl that's totally unprecedented to do  and  even further to have gone up on the  state floor and had a naturalization  ceremony  no one can argue that that is anything  but official business  uh as a backdrop to a political campaign  all of this is totally unprecedented  um it certainly in my opinion violates  the hatch act but certainly  if not the law is certainly the spirit  we want to separate  politics from government and that did  not happen last night it wasn't a  blurring of the lines  it was an erasing of the line well it  was a big night last night for melania  trump our first lady and  people on both sides of the aisle say  that she delivered that she delivered  that you know it was her job they said  to go out and humanize her husband  i'm curious about valerie starting with  you what stood out to you  in that speech it was very personal  yes it was but i don't see how one  speech can whitewash over the damage  that her husband has done over the  nearly  last four years and when she talks about  social media well who has weaponized it  more than her husband  she was the first person to call the  coronavirus corona  covid19 as opposed to the china virus  that was notable and she expressed  support and sympathy for people who have  lost their lives during the coronavirus  and that's something that we have not  heard  in the first two nights of this  convention right  well you're exactly yeah exactly  yeah um first of all i think she did a  superb job number one  she acknowledged the pandemic in a way  